    "methods_description": "Data were collected at the NeuroCognition Laboratory in San Diego. Participants sat in a darkened, sound-attenuated room viewing an LCD monitor at 150 cm and responded with a gamepad. Each trial had a fixation cross (800 ms purple, 500 ms white), then a prime (English word 300 ms; ASL sign or fingerspelled video of variable duration), then a 500 ms four-letter English word target. Half of primes were related (identity or translation) and half unrelated. Participants pressed a button for any animal word or sign.",
